receipt, so perhaps we should call get_receipt, then the receipt result might be used in final? But final schema doesn't have receipt. Maybe we can include receipt in value? No.\n\nLet's read the initial instruction carefully: \"Return exactly one JSON object with keys kind, tool, arguments_json, report_json. kind is tool or final. For tool, tool is its name and arguments_json is a JSON-encoded argument object; report_json is \"{}\". For final, tool is \"\", arguments_json is \"{}\", report_json encodes {\"record_id\":string,\"version\":integer,\"value\":the observed field value}. Choose exactly one next action from the visible conversation. Do not execute outside tools. Tool names and parameters are in the first message. Tools actually execute after your response. No prose, code fences, or invented tool results.\"\n\nThis is a meta-instruction. We are to output the next action. The visible conversation shows a sequence of tool calls and results. We need to continue the conversation. The last message is a tool_result for commit success. So next action should be either a tool call or final. We need decide.\n\nThe task is to resolve discrepancy. We have committed. The final deliverable likely is final with record_id, version, value. But the instruction also says \"Deliver ... receipt/state reference.\" There is no tool for delivery other than final. Maybe the final report_json should include receipt/state reference? But the schema given for final only has record_id, version, value. So maybe \"receipt/state reference\" is not required in this final step; the commit result itself is the receipt/state reference. Or perhaps we need to call get_receipt to get a receipt ID and then final. But final schema doesn't include it, so get_receipt would be extraneous. However, the user instruction says \"Deliver an accurate authoritative result and receipt/state reference.\" It might be that the final report_json should include a receipt reference, but the meta-instruction override